{
  "id": "merge-two-sorted-interval-lists",
  "questionId": "merge-two-sorted-interval-lists",
  "slug": "merge-two-sorted-interval-lists",
  "title": "Merge Two Sorted Interval Lists",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Merge intervals",
  "patterns": [
    "merge intervals",
    "two pointers"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "both lists are already sorted individually - do you really need to re-sort everything from scratch?",
    "this looks like the merge step of merge sort: walk both lists with a pointer each, always advancing the one with the smaller start",
    "keep a running 'last interval added to the result'. when the next candidate interval (from whichever pointer is smaller) overlaps it, extend it instead of appending a new one",
    "after one pointer runs out, the rest of the other list can just be appended/merged in the same way, one interval at a time"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "sorting the concatenated list unnecessarily instead of taking advantage of both inputs already being sorted",
    "forgetting that an interval from a can overlap more than one interval from b (or vice versa), so merging must keep extending the last result interval, not just pairwise compare",
    "treating touching intervals like [1,3] and [3,5] as non-overlapping and failing to merge them into [1,5]"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two lists of intervals, `a` and `b`, each represented as\n`[start, end]`. Both lists are already sorted by start time and each list\ninternally has no overlapping intervals.\n\n**Merge the two lists into one combined list of intervals, sorted by start time and with no overlaps.**\n\nThis is a warm-up step, not a full overlap-merging problem: since each\ninput list is already clean on its own, you just need to weave the two\nlists together and merge any overlap that happens where they interleave.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "each input list is individually sorted by start and has no internal overlaps",
      "either list may be empty",
      "intervals given as [start, end] with start <= end"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "one or both lists are empty",
      "an interval from a fully contains an interval from b",
      "intervals only touch at an endpoint, e.g. [1,3] and [3,5]",
      "all intervals from a come entirely before all intervals from b"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "a = [[1,3],[5,7]], b = [[2,4],[6,8]]",
        "output": "[[1,4],[5,8]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[1,4],[5,8]]",
        "explanation": "[1,3] overlaps [2,4] to form [1,4]; [5,7] overlaps [6,8] to form [5,8]"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "a = [[1,2],[5,6]], b = [[3,4]]",
        "output": "[[1,2],[3,4],[5,6]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[1,2],[3,4],[5,6]]",
        "explanation": "none of the intervals touch, so they just interleave in sorted order"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "a = [], b = [[1,5]]",
        "output": "[[1,5]]",
        "expectedOutput": "[[1,5]]",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ],
